  "notes": "A compound verb of {据|す}える (to set, to place) and {付|つ}ける (to attach). Describes the permanent installation or mounting of something heavy or fixed, as opposed to simply placing a portable item.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. The intransitive counterpart is {据|す}え{付|つ}く, though it is rarely used.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- エアコンを{据|す}え{付|つ}ける — to install an air conditioner\n- {機械|きかい}を{据|す}え{付|つ}ける — to install machinery\n- {据|す}え{付|つ}け{工事|こうじ} — installation work\n- {据|す}え{付|つ}け{型|がた} — built-in type, fixed type\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {設置|せっち}する — to set up, to install (more formal/official)\n- {取|と}り{付|つ}ける — to attach, to install (broader usage, including smaller items)",
